course: dictionary
lesson: 7045
title: Passion: strong feeling and strong love
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Passion is a noun. It can mean a very strong feeling, such as love, anger or excitement. It can also mean a strong love for an activity or subject. Context helps you choose the right meaning: is the sentence about feelings, a hobby, or church?
explain: «She spoke with passion» shows strong feeling in the way she talked. Passion can also be something you love doing: «a passion for football» means football is something you really enjoy.
explain: In Alice, the Mouse's face is «quite pale (with passion, Alice thought)». Here the clue is pale, and «with passion» means with strong anger, so the Mouse is very angry. Hume said «reason is the slave of the passions», meaning our strong feelings set our goals, and reason helps us reach them.
fact: Passion means a very strong feeling, such as love, anger or excitement.
fact: A passion can be a strong love for an activity or subject, like a passion for football.
fact: «With passion» means with strong feeling, as in «she spoke with passion».
fact: The Passion is the story of the suffering and death of Jesus, remembered by Christians especially at Easter.
fact: Bach wrote musical «Passions» about that story.
exercise: Ella says, «She spoke with passion.» What does passion show? | Quiet boredom | A sleepy yawn | *Strong feeling
exercise: Ben says, «My passion is drawing dragons.» What does passion mean here? | *A strong love for an activity | A cold, wet day | A very small room | The story of Jesus at Easter
exercise: In Alice, the Mouse's face is «quite pale (with passion, Alice thought)». What is the passion? | Sleepy tiredness | A cold, wet day | *Strong anger | Happy excitement
test: In «Mia has a passion for swimming», what does passion mean? | A loud noise | Lost in the woods | Very slow walking | *A strong love for an activity
test: The Passion is remembered by Christians especially at which time of year? | Bonfire Night | *Easter | Summer holidays | Christmas
exam: Hume said «reason is the slave of the passions». What does this mean? | Reason is always right and feelings never matter | *Our strong feelings set our goals, and reason helps us reach them | Passions are a kind of weather | Feelings are always wrong and must be ignored
